/-!
# Small and inner linear component exclusions

Literal full-quotient recovery, generating rank-two preimages, and the
actual A₃/C₃ systems prove original 14.7.49 and the inner branch of
14.7.51. The selected-component source leaf retains the original
14.7.48 data and earlier 14.5.21(2) commutator identity. The relative
component application uses the exact quotient and subtype conventions
of the 14.7.52 sieve. Graph and A₇ exclusions retain their independent
owners. The guarded successor uses only same-G,T earlier inputs throughout
its cubic-actor proof. In the product row, two invariant cubic lifts of
the elementary residual give the required local containment. The final
leaf applies these exclusions to the same selected component under the
multiple-overgroup guard, preserving the universal public APIs.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, refs/quasithin.pdf, 14.7.11 and 14.7.49–51,
printed pp.1045–1046 and 1064–1065.
-/
